= Factions in the PPS

These three currents are gameplay abstractions rather than formal organizations. [? if not polish_party_rules : Inherited German cards feed them through a temporary compatibility bridge until each card receives a researched Polish response. ?][? if polish_party_rules : Their strengths add up to 100; the party's dissent is their dissent weighted by strength. ?]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The parliamentary mainstream: democratic socialism, reform, workers' rights, defence of democracy and Polish independence.">Centrum PPS</span>!} strength: [+ centrum_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ centrum_dissent : dissent +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The socialist left: stronger class politics, faster economic transformation and greater openness to cooperation on the left.">Lewica PPS</span>!} strength: [+ lewica_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ lewica_dissent : dissent +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The independence and Piłsudski-oriented current: a strong state, anti-communism and state-led social reform.">Piłsudczycy</span>!} strength: [+ pilsudczycy_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ pilsudczycy_dissent : dissent +]

[? if not polish_party_rules : Affiliated trade unions — labor strength: [+ labor_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ labor_dissent : dissent +]. Labor remains a temporary inherited measure for the affiliated trade-union power centre. It is not normalized as a PPS faction and does not directly enter overall party dissent. ?]


@paramilitaries
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.polish_security_rules && Q.S && typeof PolishSecurity !== 'undefined' && PolishSecurity.ready(Q)) {
    PolishSecurity.defenseView(Q);
}
if (Q.pps_militia_strength) {
    Q.pps_militia_strength_2 = Q.pps_militia_strength.toFixed(0);
}
if (Q.rfb_strength) {
    Q.rfb_strength_2 = Q.rfb_strength.toFixed(1);
}
if (Q.sh_strength) {
    Q.sh_strength_2 = Q.sh_strength.toFixed(1);
}
if (Q.sa_strength) {
    Q.sa_strength_2 = Q.sa_strength.toFixed(1);
}
!}

